  "authoritative_metadata": "manifest.json",
  "title": "Counting on plain Pfaffian braces is #P-hard",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Counting proper 2-colourings of 3-regular 3-uniform hypergraphs whose incidence graphs are Pfaffian braces is #P-hard under polynomial-time Turing reductions. A hard plain cubic source is drawn with its vertices in distinct faces of a prism frame and every crossing replaced by a ladder site of plain cube junctions (ticket A). A bond lemma (the planarized drawing has only trivial bonds of size at most 3), ladder sites, and a cube junction lemma make the instance cyclically 4-edge-connected, hence a brace by Hall's condition; it is Pfaffian by the trisum certificate. With every site restored the count is #col(source) #col(frame). With Valiant's planar algorithm and the Heawood graph: among plain Pfaffian braces, the planar ones count in polynomial time, the knot's atom trivially, and the class is #P-hard.",
  "dependencies": [
    "PLAIN-BRACE-20261031-001A",
    "SOFT-CROSS-20261031-001B"
  ],
  "evidence_modes": [
    "construction",
    "proxy-control"
  ],
  "source_contribution": 0,
